BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Workshop Performance: “Under Light” by Naomi Qianxun Lyu 
 — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261030T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261030T200000
DTSTAMP:20261031T123911Z
UID:8c410b1c02be6324b0cf6b7f0d87@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Performing Arts\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United
  States
DESCRIPTION:This work examines how systems construct visibility and shape 
 action\, asking what it means to move within structures that determine who
  is seen\, positioned\, or valued. Drawing on the logic of chess\, the pie
 ce frames performers as both agents and instruments\, appearing to act whi
 le being shaped by a larger system. It asks what it means to be visible wh
 en movement is already scripted\, and what kind of agency is possible with
 in conditions one does not control.\nCategory: Performing Arts\nOriginal l
 isting: https://events.berkeley.edu/TDPS/event/334956-fall-workshop-perfor
 mance-under-light-by-naomi-qianxu
LOCATION:Zellerbach Hall\, Room 170\, Zellerbach Hall\, Room 170
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/TDPS/event/334956-fall-workshop-performanc
 e-under-light-by-naomi-qianxu
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: A Woman is a Woman — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261030T193000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261030T203000
DTSTAMP:20261031T123911Z
UID:dfec1041898f5f84eb2a20645410@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Jean-Luc Godard’s third feature was conceived “within the 
 framework of a neorealist musical\,” with nods to René Clair and Ernst 
 Lubitsch. Anna Karina is Angela\, an occasional stripper in a shabby club 
 called the Zodiac. She is determined to have a baby and soon\; when her lo
 ver Emile (Jean-Claude Brialy) won’t\, she turns to his friend Alfred Lu
 bitsch (Jean-Paul Belmondo)\, who will. There is magic in this film\, from
  actual hat tricks to the famous egg-frying gag to the mesmerizing traveli
 ng shots. Godard’s sense of woman as mystery is a part of that magic. (E
 ven the title throws up its hands.)\nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: ht
 tps://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328133-film-screening-a-woman-is-a-
 woman
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328133-film-screening-a-woman
 -is-a-woman
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
