END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Vivre sa vie — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261031T160000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261031T170000
DTSTAMP:20261031T123911Z
UID:38ede7569fbee762648f08955591@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Vivre sa vie depicts Nana (Anna Karina)\, a naive shopgirl\, a
 t the brief\, flickering moment when she takes responsibility for her life
 . Nana takes to the streets\, becoming a prostitute and a student of human
  emotions. Brechtian in its use of twelve dispassionately announced tablea
 ux\, Vivre sa vie is also intensely personal. Nana’s crucible is Jean-Lu
 c Godard’s existential epiphany: Nana struggles to see\, and say\, thing
 s as they are\, bravely concluding\, “All is good.” In the famous scen
 e in a movie theater\, Nana’s rapt attention to Carl Theodor Dreyer’s 
 The Passion of Joan of Arc is a tribute to another who sacrificed control 
 to take control.\nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkel
 ey.edu/BAMPFA/event/328135-film-screening-vivre-sa-vie
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328135-film-screening-vivre-s
 a-vie
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
