BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ema Nikolovska\, mezzo-soprano Sean Shibe\, guitar Orlando Variati
 ons — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261101T150000
DTSTAMP:20261031T123911Z
UID:7b2934a1a18dbbf54b80d0680fc4@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Performing Arts\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United
  States
DESCRIPTION:Mezzo-soprano Ema Nikolovska returns to Berkeley following her
  2024 debut––this time joined by acclaimed guitarist Sean Shibe––i
 n an eclectic concert weaving together acoustic and electric music across 
 genres and centuries. Orlando riffs on the character and energy of Virgini
 a Woolf’s groundbreaking novel of the same name\, with echoes of the med
 ieval Chanson de Roland and Ariosto’s Orlando Furioso . Exploring love\,
  conflict\, and identity\, the duo performs works by Schubert\, Dowland\, 
 Bob Dylan\, Laurie Anderson\, and others alongside new commissions by Sash
