DESCRIPTION:Working with trusted accomplices\, including editor Thelma Sch
 oonmaker\, cinematographer Michael Ballhaus\, actors Robert De Niro and Jo
 e Pesci\, and brilliant first-time collaborators Ray Liotta and Lorraine B
 racco\, Martin Scorsese combines varied cinematic styles\, camera techniqu
 es\, and a precisely executed collage of popular music\, adapting Nicholas
  Pileggi’s chronicle of real-life Mafia associate Henry Hill. Hurtling t
 hrough some twenty-five years of “family” life\, the riveting Liotta g
 ives voice to Hill’s chilling and funny first-person account. As focused
  on quotidian details as on dramatic moments\, Scorsese wanted the movie t
 o have a documentary feel\, “as if you had 16mm cameras with thes\nCateg
